# ============================================================
# فروشگاه من (Online Store) — Environment Variables
# ============================================================
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.
#
# ⚠️  THIS IS A TEMPLATE — IT MUST CONTAIN NO REAL SECRETS.
#     Every value below is a placeholder. Production credentials belong in
#     .env.local (gitignored) or in the hosting panel's environment settings.
#     A `.env.example` gets committed, shared and reviewed; treating it as a
#     scratch copy of the real environment is how credentials leak.
#
# Required vars will crash the app if missing.

# --- MongoDB (Required) ---
# Connection string for MongoDB. Database name: marlooai
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://<user>:<password>@<host>:<port>/?authSource=admin

# --- NextAuth (Required) ---
# Secret key for JWT encryption. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=replace-with-openssl-rand-base64-32
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Optional: Telegram Bot Integration ---
# Telegram Bot Token from @BotFather (required for supplier/admin notifications)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=000000000:replace-with-botfather-token
# Numeric chat ID for admin Telegram notifications (get it from @userinfobot)
ADMIN_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=000000000

# --- Optional: Analytics ---
# Google Analytics Measurement ID
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# --- Zarinpal Payment Gateway ---
# REQUIRED for online payment. Get your Merchant ID from https://zarinpal.com
# In production, use your real merchant ID. In development, use a sandbox merchant ID.
# The system automatically uses sandbox API when NODE_ENV=development.
ZARINPAL_MERCHANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# --- SMS OTP Authentication (Session 62) ---
# OTP login/registration codes. Development and CI use the hermetic mock seam
# (SMS_MOCK=1 — same philosophy as ZARINPAL_MOCK); NO sms.ir account or
# credentials are needed for development.
# Production: set BOTH SMS_IR_API_KEY + SMS_IR_TEMPLATE_ID (sms.ir panel) and
# the provider activates; while either is missing the OTP request API returns
# a controlled 503 (local development is never broken).
# SMS_MOCK=1
# SMS_IR_API_KEY=your-sms-ir-api-key
# SMS_IR_TEMPLATE_ID=123456

# --- E2E Testing (Playwright, dev-only) ---
# When set to 1 (dev only), the Zarinpal gateway is mocked: requestPayment
# returns a same-origin stub verify URL and verifyPayment returns a fixed
# success — the payment E2E journey runs hermetically without the interactive
# sandbox page. NEVER set in production (src/lib/zarinpal.ts also gates on
# NODE_ENV === "development").
# ZARINPAL_MOCK=1

# --- CI/CD (GitHub Actions, Session 60) ---
# The hermetic `ci.yml` workflow (static + unit + e2e + production build) needs
# NO env vars/secrets: it boots a fresh MongoDB service container and the dev
# server with ZARINPAL_MOCK=1 (CI-only NEXTAUTH_SECRET/NEXTAUTH_URL and
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL are inlined in the workflow).
#
# The optional nightly `regression.yml` (50 real-API suites) DOES need the
# real sandbox/S3/Telegram values. Add these as GitHub repository secrets
# (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions) — same names as below:
#   ZARINPAL_MERCHANT_ID   (sandbox merchant id)
#   ZARINPAL_CALLBACK_URL   (optional — only if you override the derived callback)
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN
#   ADMIN_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
#   LIARA_ENDPOINT / LIARA_BUCKET_NAME / LIARA_ACCESS_KEY / LIARA_SECRET_KEY / LIARA_REGION
# The workflow self-skips until ZARINPAL_MERCHANT_ID is set.

# --- Application URL (Required for Payment + SEO) ---
# IMPORTANT: Set this to your real production domain when deployed.
# Used for:
#   - Zarinpal payment callback URL (where Zarinpal redirects after payment)
#   - Sitemap, metadata, and canonical URLs
# Local development: http://localhost:3000
# Production example: https://mystore.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional: Override the Zarinpal callback URL explicitly.
# If not set, the system derives it from NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL + "/api/payment/verify"
# You typically do NOT need to set this — let the system derive it.
# ZARINPAL_CALLBACK_URL=

# --- Optional: Admin Seed (first-time setup) ---
# Used by scripts/seed-admin.js to create the default administrator.
# These are only read by the seed script, not by the application.
# ADMIN_SEED_PHONE=09120000000
# ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD=admin123456
# ADMIN_SEED_NAME=مدیر سیستم

# --- Object storage (Liara S3) — product & description images (Optional) ---
# While any of these is missing, uploads fail with a controlled 503 instead of
# breaking the app (src/lib/env.ts lists them as optional).
LIARA_ENDPOINT=https://<bucket-name>.storage.iran.liara.space
LIARA_BUCKET_NAME=your-bucket-name
LIARA_ACCESS_KEY=your-liara-access-key
LIARA_SECRET_KEY=your-liara-secret-key
LIARA_REGION=us-west-2

# --- Legacy (NOT read by the application) ---
# JWT_SECRET appears in no source file — NextAuth signing uses NEXTAUTH_SECRET.
# Kept commented so the historical key is not mistaken for a live one.
# JWT_SECRET=

# ============================================================
# Deployment & runtime (Session 89)
# ============================================================
# The production runtime is a plain Node server:
#
#     npm ci && npm run build && npm start      # start = `next start`
#
# Chabokan's "NextJs" cloud-hosting service runs exactly those package.json
# scripts (build + start) and holds every variable below in its service
# dashboard — so this repo needs NO platform manifest (no vercel.json, no
# Dockerfile). See README.md → "Deployment".
#
# PORT — port the app listens on. Chabokan defaults to 3000 (set it in the
# service dashboard); `next start` honours this variable.
# PORT=3000
#
# NODE_ENV — set to "production" automatically by `next start`. Do NOT set it
# in the dashboard, it is not a knob.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL — MUST be an absolute http(s) origin in production. The
# build FAILS FAST if it is missing or malformed (src/lib/constants.ts), because
# canonical URLs, the sitemap, OG/JSON-LD and the Zarinpal callback are all
# derived from it.
#
# Health probe — point the platform's health check / uptime monitor at:
#     GET /api/health
#   → 200 {"status":"ok","db":"up",...} when the app and MongoDB are ready;
#   → 503 {"status":"degraded","db":"down",...} when the database is not
#     reachable (bounded to ~4s, never hangs, exposes no credentials).
#
# Post-deploy check — verify the production path without touching data:
#     node scripts/verify-deployment.js
